From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: pass GEA direction as the declared enum

The upstream Makefile compiles the .c fixtures with g++. Its GEA fixture
passes an int directly to functions declared with gprs_cipher_direction,
which modern C++ rejects. Cast the two test arguments after retaining the
fixture's existing 0/1 values. This keeps all GEA vectors in %check.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V review of the official v4.0.0 archive
Patch-License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Remove-When: An upstream release uses the declared direction enum in the
 GEA fixture or otherwise makes the fixture compile as C++.
---
 gea_test.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gea_test.c b/gea_test.c
--- a/gea_test.c
+++ b/gea_test.c
@@ -23,6 +23,6 @@ void test_gea3(uint64_t kc, uint32_t iv, int dir, uint16_t len, char * res) {
 void test_gea3(uint64_t kc, uint32_t iv, int dir, uint16_t len, char * res) {
     printf("%d: %d -> 0x%X ", len, dir, iv);
     uint8_t out[len];
-    osmo_gea3(out, len, kc, iv, dir);
+    osmo_gea3(out, len, kc, iv, (enum gprs_cipher_direction)dir);
     print_check(res, out, len);
 }
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ void test_gea4(char * kc, uint32_t iv, int dir, uint16_t len, char * res) {
 void test_gea4(char * kc, uint32_t iv, int dir, uint16_t len, char * res) {
     printf("%d: %d -> 0x%X ", len, dir, iv);
     uint8_t out[len], ck[256];
     osmo_hexparse(kc, ck, len);
-    osmo_gea4(out, len, ck, iv, dir);
+    osmo_gea4(out, len, ck, iv, (enum gprs_cipher_direction)dir);
     print_check(res, out, len);
 }
